<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    What Android's own backup takes on API 30 and below. API 31 and above use
    data_extraction_rules.xml instead.

    The Room database and the DataStore preferences are the whole of the user's data, and naming
    them is what makes that a decision rather than whatever the defaults happen to cover. The
    database domain is taken whole: Room journals in WAL mode, so the `-wal` and `-shm` files
    alongside `LiftApp.db` can hold writes the `.db` file does not have yet.

    Nothing else is worth carrying. The muscle bitmap cache is regenerated on demand, and the
    directory the share action writes to holds a copy of what is already in the database.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include
        domain="database"
        path="." />
    <include
        domain="file"
        path="datastore/" />
</full-backup-content>
